-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_hookio_stream_writes.adam - the write side of System.HookIO from C
  (PaskalCPP's std_hookio TestStreamWrites)

  The C fixture's write sequences (std_hookio_c_writes: buffered fputc /
  fwrite / fputs and their flushes, read / write turns, ftell with bytes
  pending, fclose with no fflush, and what another reader sees after each
  step) on a virtual file and on a real file of the same bytes, through
  every write mode, text and binary (a text handle writes each '\n' as
  "\r\n"): every slot equals the real file's. A variant C leaves
  undefined (a write right after a read, a read or ungetc right after a
  write) runs on the update modes only, twice: the handle with the
  undefined sequence, then with the call C requires made, each against the
  real file with that call made. One line per case: ok when every check
  of it held, else a FAIL line per check that did not.
  The setvbuf variants (3, 4, 5) come with setvbuf, the fprintf variant
  (6) with the printf family.
*******************************************************************************/

